0322: Wi-Fi: kern.sweet_wifid_opened (wifid read RSSI_BOUNDS: com.sapphire.wifidkick restarts wifid only if it is 0 at 25 s;
a wifid restarted when it was fine sat ~4.5 min before using en0); the scan table drops APs not heard for 120 s and
recycles the oldest when full (with 64 BSSIDs heard no new network was listed or joinable). Tester bugs 6 and 7.

--- a/bsd/dev/sapphire_apple80211.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sapphire_apple80211.c
@@ -47,6 +47,16 @@
 #include <sys/sapphire_sta.h>
 #include <sys/sockio.h>
 #include <sys/systm.h>
+#include <sys/sysctl.h>
+
+/*
+ * 0322: how many times wifid has read the RSSI bounds, i.e. opened the device and gone on to power and
+ * scan. com.sapphire.wifidkick reads it 25 s into the boot and restarts wifid only if it is still 0
+ * (a wifid restarted when it was fine sat ~4.5 min before touching en0 again).
